<section xml:id="sec-pretext-cheat-sheet">
    <title>PreTeXt Cheat Sheet</title>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            <tag>202606012315</tag> |
            <tag>pretext</tag> <tag>xml</tag> <tag>authoring</tag>
        </p>
        <p>
            A comprehensive guide to PreTeXt XML elements and structure for authoring mathematical content.
        </p>
    </introduction>

    <subsection xml:id="sub-pretext-structure">
        <title>Document Structure</title>
        <p>
            PreTeXt documents follow a strict hierarchical organization.
        </p>
        <program language="xml">
            <code>
                <![CDATA[
<pretext>
  <docinfo> ... </docinfo>
  <book xml:id="my-book">
    <title>Book Title</title>
    <chapter xml:id="ch-demo">
      <title>Chapter</title>
      <section xml:id="sec-demo">
        <title>Section Title</title>
        <introduction>
          <p>
            <tag>202606012315</tag> |
            <tag>topic</tag>
          </p>
        </introduction>
        <subsection xml:id="sub-demo">
          <title>Subsection</title>
          <p>Content with <m>E=mc^2</m> and <xref ref="ch-demo"/>.</p>
        </subsection>
        <conclusion>
          <p>🖇️ <alert>Linked Notes:</alert> <xref ref="other-note"/></p>
        </conclusion>
      </section>
    </chapter>
  </book>
</pretext>
                ]]>
            </code>
        </program>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="sub-pretext-inline">
        <title>Inline Elements and Tags</title>
        <p>
            Inline elements are used within paragraphs (<c><![CDATA[<p>]]></c>) to style text or add semantics.
        </p>
        <table>
            <title>Common Inline Elements</title>
            <tabular bottom="minor" top="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
                <row header="yes">
                    <cell>Element</cell>
                    <cell>Usage</cell>
                    <cell>Example</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<m>]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Inline Math (LaTeX)</cell>
                    <cell><m>E = mc^2</m></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<tag>]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Semantic Tags (Metadata)</cell>
                    <cell><tag>quantum mechanics</tag></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<c>]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Inline Code/Verbatim</cell>
                    <cell><c>git status</c></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<em>]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Emphasis (Cooler Blue/Italic)</cell>
                    <cell><em>Nuance</em></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<term>]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Defining a term (Orange Gradient)</cell>
                    <cell><term>Bivector</term></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<strong>]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Strong emphasis (Prominent Cyan)</cell>
                    <cell><strong>Key Term</strong></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<alert>]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Metadata labels (Glassmorphic Pill)</cell>
                    <cell><alert>Warning!</alert></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<em class="alert">]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Critical Emphasis (Blue Gradient)</cell>
                    <cell><em class="alert">Important!</em></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<xref>]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Cross-reference</cell>
                    <cell>See <xref ref="sec-pretext-cheat-sheet" /></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell><c><![CDATA[<url>]]></c></cell>
                    <cell>Hyperlink</cell>
                    <cell><url href="https://pretextbook.org">PreTeXt</url></cell>
                </row>
            </tabular>
        </table>
        <p>
            <alert>Note:</alert> In this project, <c><![CDATA[<tag>]]></c> elements are styled as glassmorphic pills.
        </p>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="sub-pretext-math">
        <title>Mathematics</title>
        <p>
            PreTeXt supports various math environments using standard LaTeX notation.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <title>Inline Math</title>
                <p>Use <c><![CDATA[<m>...</m>]]></c> for inline expressions.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <title>Single Line Equations</title>
                <p>Use <c><![CDATA[<md>]]></c> for equations. Single-line equations no longer use <c><![CDATA[<me>]]></c> or <c><![CDATA[<men>]]></c> (deprecated). Use <c>@number="yes"</c> on <c><![CDATA[<md>]]></c> for numbering.</p>
                <program language="xml">
                    <code>
                        <![CDATA[<md number="yes">
    <mrow xml:id="eq-schrodinger">i\hbar\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\Psi = \hat{H}\Psi</mrow>
</md>]]>
                    </code>
                </program>
                <p>
                    <alert>Output:</alert>
                    <md number="yes">
                        <mrow xml:id="eq-schrodinger-example">i\hbar\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\Psi = \hat{H}\Psi</mrow>
                    </md>
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <title>Aligned Equations</title>
                <p>Use <c><![CDATA[<md>]]></c> with <c><![CDATA[<mrow>]]></c> for multiple lines. Use <c><![CDATA[\amp]]></c> for alignment.</p>
                <program language="xml">
                    <code>
                        <![CDATA[
        <md>
          <mrow> \nabla \cdot \mathbf{E} \amp = \frac{\rho}{\epsilon_0} </mrow>
          <mrow> \nabla \cdot \mathbf{B} \amp = 0 </mrow>
        </md>
                        ]]>
                    </code>
                </program>
                <p>
                    <alert>Output:</alert>
                    <md>
                        <mrow> \nabla \cdot \mathbf{E} \amp = \frac{\rho}{\epsilon_0} </mrow>
                        <mrow> \nabla \cdot \mathbf{B} \amp = 0 </mrow>
                    </md>
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
        </subsection>

        <subsection xml:id="sub-pretext-blocks">
        <title>Common Blocks</title>
        <p>
            Structural blocks organize content into logical units with specific styling.
        </p>
        <program language="xml">
            <code>
                <![CDATA[
        <definition xml:id="def-unitary">
          <title>Unitary Operator</title>
          <statement>
            <p>An operator <m>U</m> is unitary if <m>U^\dagger U = I</m>.</p>
          </statement>
        </definition>
                ]]>
            </code>
        </program>
        <p>
            <alert>Output:</alert>
        </p>
        <definition xml:id="def-unitary-example">
            <title>Unitary Operator</title>
            <statement>
                <p>An operator <m>U</m> is unitary if <m>U^\dagger U = I</m>.</p>
            </statement>
        </definition>

        <program language="xml">
            <code>
                <![CDATA[
        <theorem xml:id="thm-noether">
          <title>Noether's Theorem</title>
          <statement>
            <p>Every differentiable symmetry ... has a corresponding conservation law.</p>
          </statement>
        </theorem>
                ]]>
            </code>
        </program>
        <p>
            <alert>Output:</alert>
        </p>
        <theorem xml:id="thm-noether-example">
            <title>Noether's Theorem</title>
            <statement>
                <p>Every differentiable symmetry ... has a corresponding conservation law.</p>
            </statement>
        </theorem>

        <program language="xml">
            <code>
                <![CDATA[
        <assemblage>
          <title>Key Concept</title>
          <p>Assemblages are used for boxed summaries (Glassmorphic in this theme).</p>
        </assemblage>
                ]]>
            </code>
        </program>
        <p>
            <alert>Output:</alert>
        </p>
        <assemblage>
            <title>Key Concept</title>
            <p>Assemblages are used for boxed summaries (Glassmorphic in this theme).</p>
        </assemblage>
        </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="sub-pretext-elements-table">
        <title>Comprehensive Element Table</title>
        <table>
            <title>PreTeXt Element Categories</title>
            <tabular bottom="minor" top="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
                <row header="yes">
                    <cell>Category</cell>
                    <cell>Elements</cell>
                    <cell>Description</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>Structure</cell>
                    <cell><c>book</c>, <c>part</c>, <c>chapter</c>, <c>section</c></cell>
                    <cell>High-level document organization</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>Blocks</cell>
                    <cell><c>definition</c>, <c>theorem</c>, <c>example</c></cell>
                    <cell>Semantic mathematical environments</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>Admonitions</cell>
                    <cell><c>note</c>, <c>warning</c>, <c>insight</c>, <c>remark</c></cell>
                    <cell>Side-bars or callout boxes</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>Technical</cell>
                    <cell><c>program</c>, <c>image</c>, <c>table</c>, <c>figure</c></cell>
                    <cell>Non-textual data, code, and graphics</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>Lists</cell>
                    <cell><c>ul</c>, <c>ol</c>, <c>dl</c></cell>
                    <cell>Unordered, ordered, and description lists</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>Backmatter</cell>
                    <cell><c>idx</c>, <c>biblio</c>, <c>glossary</c>, <c>colophon</c></cell>
                    <cell>Indices, references, and metadata</cell>
                </row>
            </tabular>
        </table>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="sub-project-conventions">
        <title>Project Conventions</title>
        <p>
            Custom styles and standards used in this Zettelkasten.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <p>
                    <alert>Note Metadata:</alert> Every note should include a metadata block (Note ID, Tags, etc.). This block can be placed in <c><![CDATA[<introduction>]]></c>, <c><![CDATA[<blockquote>]]></c>, <c><![CDATA[<aside>]]></c>, or <c><![CDATA[<paragraphs>]]></c>.
                </p>
                <program language="xml">
                    <code>
                        <![CDATA[
<!-- Traditional Introduction -->
<introduction>
  <p>
    <tag>202606012315</tag> |
    <tag>topic1</tag> <tag>topic2</tag>
  </p>
</introduction>

<!-- Alternative using Blockquote (Always visible, no title) -->
<blockquote>
  <p>
    <tag>202606012315</tag> |
    <tag>topic1</tag>
  </p>
</blockquote>
                        ]]>
                    </code>
                </program>
                <p>
                    <alert>Output (approximate):</alert>
                </p>
                <blockquote>
                    <p>
                        <tag>202606012315</tag> | <tag>topic1</tag>, <tag>topic2</tag> | <alert>PreFigure Demo:</alert><tag>🔗 Interactive</tag>
                    </p>
                </blockquote>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    <alert>Note IDs:</alert> Use <c>YYYYMMDDNNNN</c> or <c>HHMM</c> format.
                    The first <c><![CDATA[<tag>]]></c> in a supported metadata block (Introduction, Blockquote, etc.) is automatically styled as a purple glassmorphic Note ID.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    <alert>Conclusion Metadata:</alert> Conclusions use <c><![CDATA[<alert>]]></c> tags for metadata labels (e.g., Linked Notes, References), which are automatically styled as blue glassmorphic pills.
                </p>
                <program language="xml">
                    <code>
                        <![CDATA[
<conclusion>
  <p>
    🖇️ <alert>Linked Notes:</alert> <xref ref="sec-topic" />
  </p>
  <p>
    🔖 <alert>References:</alert> <xref ref="biblio-item" />
  </p>
</conclusion>
                        ]]>
                    </code>
                </program>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    <alert>List Titles:</alert> Headings inside list items (e.g. <c><![CDATA[<li><title>...</title></li>]]></c> or <c><![CDATA[<li class="li"><title>...</title></li>]]></c>) are styled in prominent cyan with the heading font.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    <alert>Assemblages:</alert> Use for primary takeaways or "atomic" notes within a section.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </subsection>

</section>
